            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MIROC5",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "Chikira and Sugiyama cumulus scheme",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "We found that the perturbations in the single parameter of the newly developed cumulus scheme (Chikira and Sugiyama 2010) drove the significant sensitivity of the middle-level cloud albedo feedback.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MIROC5",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "Normalized Cloud Index",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "Here, we define the metric that measures the meridional contrast of middle-level cloud albedo in the C-CTL runs according to Watanabe et al. (2011a):\nA indicates the middle-level cloud albedo averaged over the area of the north black box in Fig. 11a (120\u00b0W, 180\u00b0W, 7\u00b0N, 12\u00b0N).\nB is the average over the area of the south black box (120\u00b0W, 180\u00b0W, 12.5\u00b0S, 2.5\u00b0S).\nThe Normalized Cloud Index (NCI) is defined as (B \u2013 A)/(B + A).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MIROC5",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "Normalized Precipitation Index",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The Normalized Precipitation Index (NPI), which measures the meridional contrast of precipitation, is defined similarly to NCI. The standard deviation of the annual mean SST averaged over the Nino 3.4 region (170\u00b0E, 120\u00b0W, 5\u00b0S, 5\u00b0N) is considered to be the metric of the ENSO amplitude.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": false
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "El Ni\u00f1o-Southern Oscillation",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Pacific ITCZ",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "A wetter atmosphere over the southern part of the Pacific ITCZ increases precipitation anomalies related to the El Ni\u00f1o-Southern Oscillation (ENSO) (i.e., stronger Bjerknes feedback; Watanabe et al. 2011a), which results in higher amplitudes of the ENSO (Fig. 12b).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MIROC3",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SUBSEQUENT_VERSION",
            "target_entity_instance": "MIROC5",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "Although the CS of MIROC5 PPE is low (2.2\u20133.2 \u00b0C), the CS within the PPE of MIROC3 ASGCM (an old version of MIROC) is high (>4 \u00b0C) (Annan et al. 2005).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        }
